-- title:
--   From HTo G Self Consistency Q SDDCore Bound
-- statement:
--   **G-hat self-consistency gives a uniform left-right qSDD bound.** Let $\psi$ be the two-register state, let $F$ be the indexed polynomial family, and let $\zeta$ be an error. Assume the completed G-hat left and right families satisfy the stated self-consistency relation with error derived from $\zeta$. For every natural $n$, let $\mathcal U$ be the uniform distribution on a field point and an $n$-tuple, write $U_{x,g}$ for the indexed head effect, and let $L$ and $R$ denote left and right tensor placement. Then
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E_{(x,\mathbf x)\sim\mathcal U}
--   \operatorname{qSDDCore}_\psi\!\left(
--   g\mapsto L(U_{x,g}),
--   g\mapsto R(U_{x,g})
--   \right)\le2\zeta.
--   $$
--
--   The conclusion is the explicit self-consistency contribution used in the sandwich context and adjacent-stage error estimates.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_selfConsistency_qSDDCore_bound`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
